  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "Type_ProfileSequenceId_Write",
    "file": "lcms/src/cmstypes.c",
    "description": "Type_ProfileSequenceId_Write trusts Seq->n from a previously parsed cmsSEQ object and passes it to WritePositionTable, which iterates i=0..Seq->n-1 and accesses Seq->seq[i] via WriteSeqID without validating that the seq array actually has Seq->n elements. In this PoV, the cmsSEQ is inconsistent/corrupted (n larger than allocated entries), so WriteSeqID reads Seq->seq[n].Description out of bounds, causing the ASan heap-buffer-overflow at cmstypes.c:3522.",
    "conditions": "In cms_profile_fuzzer, attacker-controlled ICC bytes are opened, a tag is read (cmsReadTag on gamut), then the profile is saved (cmsSaveProfileToFile). The crafted profile must cause a cmsSigProfileSequenceIdType/cmsSEQ object with mismatched internal state (Seq->n inflated relative to allocated seq entries) to be present when saving tags. During serialization, Type_ProfileSequenceId_Write uses that unchecked Seq->n, and WritePositionTable/WriteSeqID index past the seq allocation, triggering OOB read."
  },
